A||||7||Bluebottlejunky||Prep for shows? What do you guys do?||||1||
Z||000000||Bluebottlejunky||05-02-2001||08:36 PM||||Hey everyone with all the cool fiero shows coming up this summer..what do you guys do to make your car looks SWEET? any tips?  Also anyone got any good tips on getting out a little grease stain on my seats?<BR>THANKS<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp, <BR>AOL IM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000001||Old Lar||05-02-2001||08:51 PM||||Wash it<BR>Clean it<BR>Polish it<BR>Wax it<P>Meguires 4 step<P>Grease: upholstry cleaner, I have had luck with some diluted Simple Green.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Robert||05-02-2001||09:24 PM||||I picked this up at last years WestFeast in San Diego from the winner of the custom modified class.  Anything “Back to Black” works.  I use Mothers myself; I don’t think it maters on the brand.  If you read the label it says its good for anything that is dull black.  There are many things on a Fiero that are dull black i.e.: most things in the engine compartment, under the hood, and I find it works well at restoring the gloss to the trunk release button on the dash.  The best way to use this stuff is to put a small amount on a paintbrush, and apply it to whatever.  Then wipe the excess off.  The paintbrush will get in all the nooks and crannies. <BR>As far as wax, I have discovered this site recommended by the Mustang group I also belong to. <A HREF="http://www.zainobros.com/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.zainobros.com/</A>   <BR>They swear by this stuff, but I have not used it myself. Has anyone here used it?  I will be giving it a try soon.<P>Hope this helps<P>Robert<BR><P>------------------<BR>           <IMG SRC="http://canterburytrails.com/photo/T2.GIF">  <P> "By the time you die, you should be so used to <BR>paying taxes that it would be almost second nature <BR>to you."<P>Will Rogers, U.S. Writer and Humorist||||reg||1
Z||000003||FieroJoe||05-02-2001||09:31 PM||||The best tire product I have used is Meguiar's Endurance Tire Gel.  It actually lasts and works like it says it does, typical of Meguiar's products.  For the interior vinyl I use Meguiar's #40, cleans the crap off and gives a great shine and good smell too.<P>Also, if you can get access to a pressure washer, you can really clean up an engine compartment and front compartment with one of those, and then of course put some sort of protectant on anything black plastic.<P>------------------<BR>AIM: FieroJoe87<BR>87 Coupe 5spd<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bluebottlejunky||05-02-2001||10:04 PM||||So I can goto any car wash and clean my engine bay?  I have seen it on the car wash to select the Enginebay clean thing..I always thought it would be bad for the cars wiring?<P>Im gunna have to try that tire gel...but so far the 4 step waxs/polishs seem great..!<P>------------------<BR>Mike<BR>85'GT 4sp, <BR>AOL IM: Fierofanatic2001||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroLisa||05-02-2001||10:28 PM||||Since I have a new paint job, I just use a polish to shine my car up<P>But as for the rest of it: I never really let the interior get dirty, but when it gets dusty I just wipe it with a damp cloth. I vacuum the carpet or wash it if necessary. <P>Engine: Its not a daily driver so once again it doesn't get too terribly dirty between shows, but I use a tire cleaning foam and then a tire shine to get all the dull black things shiny and pretty. <P>I have that Mothers Back to Black for the black molding on the outside of my car.<P>I clean my rims with windex and use a toothbrush to get the crap out of the tread of my tires for big shows. <P>I've been known to dig out the tweezers to get the pine needles and crap out of tiny places.<P>Basically I sit on my butt for  along time and clean. I have a suitcase full of cleaning implements I keep in my trunk.<P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 violet pearl 4 speed GT- 17 in. rims, lowered, cold-air,<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><P><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/ncfieros/" TARGET=_blank>Tarheels Fieros Website</A>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Hartz||05-02-2001||11:12 PM||||I've used Zaino on my Firehawk.  The f-body guys also swear by this stuff.  Heck, if Mustang and F-body guys can actually AGREE on something, it's got to be good, right?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>It's a bit pricey, but "if you have the means, I'd highly recommend it."<P>Hartz<BR>'84 SC 5.7L V8<BR>'85 SE 3.1L V6 Turbo||||reg||14
Z||000007||rogergarrison||05-02-2001||11:17 PM||||windex is good for everything from glass to bugs across the front. Polish thats OK to put on in sun, an upholstery brush for seats and carpet, and WD 40 to make the engine look all clean n shiny. I like the Endurance tire dressing too, lasts for weeks, dont have that phony wet super high gloss shine.<P>bluebottle, car wash is ok for engine, just try not to spray directly on distributor, sensors like MAP, TPS, and all the little relays on firewall and by the battery. getting them wet wont hurt, just dont soak them down hard. Also I found out spraying the alternator down very hard can blow it too.<p>[This message has been edited by rogergarrison (edited 05-02-2001).]||||reg||1
